L553: ## cite44†Security L554: 
L555: The maintainers of OpenZeppelin Contracts for Cairo are mainly concerned with the correctness and security of the code as published in the library.
L556: Customizing implementations and manipulating the component state may break some important assumptions and introduce vulnerabilities. While we try to ensure the components remain secure in the face of a wide range of potential customizations, this is done in a best-effort manner. Any and all customizations to the component logic should be carefully reviewed and checked against the source code of the component they are customizing so as to fully understand their impact and guarantee their security.
